    "created_at": "2026-11-19T17:39:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T17:39:20Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/2474-wcs-flip-z-refusal · PR #2785 · pinned by a_flipped_z_refuses_by_name, a_flipped_z_without_a_cycle_names_the_tool_length_word_only, a_flipped_z_refuses_the_post_by_name · merges when reviewed\n\nThe PR keeps the refusal of a flipped Z. It makes the refusal name the exact reason, and it records the decision in `docs/decisions/2474-wcs-flip-z-refusal.md`. This is the second \"Done means\" clause.\n\nThe reason: on a control that reads Z reversed, a preset tool length needs G44 and a touched-off tool length needs G43. The project does not state which. The wrong word moves the tool by twice its length.\n\nA carry of Z needs one new statement from the user: how the tool lengths are measured. The maintainer decides if that work is wanted.\n",
